  "title": "Mosaic_Pompeii_Floors / all 46 mosaic floors to walk on, framed by the scaffold, and the five Pompeii floors on raised decks",
  "about": "Palle, 2026-11-02: 'mosaics inside the playground scaffolding'. Each mosaic is a plate place at y 1 with its floor in the slot - the plate is what you stand on (the mosaic floors carry no collision of their own), the rim and rails are the scaffold. Tested inside the map's own trial before it moves to the skyscraper. 2026-11-02, Palle: 'can I walk all floors - I mean the mosaic floors'. The field: every mosaic floor artifact in commons/artifacts/pompeii_mosaic_floor (46) on a 4 x 4 m floor board, framed by the kit's bars, fitted, with a walk body at its surface (the floors carry no collision of their own) and its name at the south edge; density three times each script's one-metre default. The five decks stand north of it.",
